id reference."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"content","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for Lyric."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"endsLine","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether this lyric ends a line, per RP-017 for Standard MIDI File Lyric meta-events. Used to facilitate lyric display for Karaoke and similar applications."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"endsParagraph","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether this lyric ends a paragraph, per RP-017 for Standard MIDI File Lyric meta-events. Used to facilitate lyric display for Karaoke and similar applications."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"footnote","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The footnote element specifies editorial information that appears in footnotes in the printed score. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"level","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The level element specifies editorial information for different MusicXML elements. It is defined within a group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"number","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Identifies this lyric among multiple lines, such as when the same lyric applies to both a stem-up and a stem-down voice."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"name","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An alternative to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"number"},{"type":"text","text":" for identifying this lyric among multiple lines. Common values are verse and chorus."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"justify","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The justify attribute is used to indicate left, center, or right justification. The default value varies for different elements. For elements where the justify attribute is present but the halign attribute is not, the justify attribute indicates horizontal alignment as well as justification."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"position","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For most elements, any program will compute a default x and y position. The position attributes let this be changed two ways."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"placement","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement attribute indicates whether something is above or below another element, such as a note or a notation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"color","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"printsObject","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether to print an object (e.g. a note or a rest). Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" if not specified."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"timeOnly","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Restricts the element to apply to a specific set of times through a repeated section."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/init(id:content:endsline:endsparagraph:footnote:level:number:name:justify:position:placement:color:printsobject:timeonly:)"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/init(id:content:endsLine:endsParagraph:footnote:level:number:name:justify:position:placement:color:printsObject:timeOnly:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Initializer","title":"init(id:content:endsLine:endsParagraph:footnote:level:number:name:justify:position:placement:color:printsObject:timeOnly:)","symbolKind":"init","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLyricV2id7content8endsLine0F9Paragraph8footnote5level6number4name7justify8position9placement5color12printsObjec